    "text": "To determine how many slices of pizza James ate, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of pizza slices.\n2. Determine what fraction of the total slices James ate.\n3. Calculate the number of slices James ate based on the fraction.\n\nFirst, we calculate the total number of pizza slices. Since each pizza has 6 slices and there are 2 pizzas, the total number of slices is:\n\\[ 6 \\text{ slices/pizza} \\times 2 \\text{ pizzas} = 12 \\text{ slices} \\]\n\nNext, we need to find out what fraction of the total slices James ate. James ate \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\) of all the slices. Therefore, the number of slices James ate is:\n\\[ \\frac{2}{3} \\times 12 \\text{ slices} = \\frac{2 \\times 12}{3} = \\frac{24}{3} = 8 \\text{ slices} \\]\n\nSo, the number of slices of pizza that James ate is \\(\\boxed{8}\\).",
